{"id": "EUVD-2026-93312", "enisaUuid": "bd77a0e1-ca63-3e80-ab95-a594e581c389", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: mesh: reset the CSA state when leaving\n\nifmsh->csa is allocated in ieee80211_mesh_csa_beacon() and only freed\nin ieee80211_mesh_finish_csa(), i.e. when the channel switch completes.\nLeaving the mesh while a switch is still pending therefore leaks it.\n\nAdditionally, ifmsh->csa_role and ifmsh->chsw_ttl have their state leak\nin this case, so things can get mixed up in addition to the memory\nleak.\n\nRefactor the reset and call it in ieee80211_stop_mesh() to fix it all.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:46:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:17:37", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aba8dfb45864441199748c33ce3c1c8ca121c8bd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bd3b21145ae2e781daac1bbd19216a63ab4e0cbd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ba5bf83a81e8832cb84bb3a2da67512f81f57a02", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/860134b3af77970e006feab7e5decb8c84771c7f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6v32-hcc5-q9w8", "CVE-2026-98327"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "26a94e8a-1257-3343-968c-dfa200864aea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b8456a14e9d2770846fcf74de18ff95b676149a3 <ba5bf83a81e8832cb84bb3a2da67512f81f57a02"}, {"id": "2ae606d0-59d4-3de7-8604-659e4741ce9a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b8456a14e9d2770846fcf74de18ff95b676149a3 <bd3b21145ae2e781daac1bbd19216a63ab4e0cbd"}, {"id": "2b0dc384-b8d9-3421-a764-c976aae19823", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b8456a14e9d2770846fcf74de18ff95b676149a3 <860134b3af77970e006feab7e5decb8c84771c7f"}, {"id": "525de643-51d4-3d32-b1ba-1ca6a3e06dfb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "54e62689-88e1-3766-a0ee-887ce026d3d2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "74180b6d-aea8-3a4b-9496-1571182f2340", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "8c4d59fe-41fe-396c-aa8a-b441e8583fb5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "94d84f73-1264-3930-9e43-be6ae7a9dbcb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b8456a14e9d2770846fcf74de18ff95b676149a3 <aba8dfb45864441199748c33ce3c1c8ca121c8bd"}, {"id": "a0c1ebfa-7fdf-3c14-83ec-fc18cb66b162", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.13"}, {"id": "a15bc498-123a-3a26-975b-eec1d8f46e37", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4388eef7-32a7-3176-bc3b-54a0b2596ca4", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}